  "title": "Agent runs get a more honest Pollen estimate",
  "summary": "A day of making existing things more legible: agent costs, community publishing, model routes, docs, and metrics.\n\nAgent calls are now grouped with their model steps and tool calls when calculating public cost estimates, balance checks, and price sorting. A free-looking wrapper no longer makes a Pollen-consuming run look free. Separately, text generations that end with an upstream error are recorded as failures rather than billed as successful generations.\n\nGuides now explain how to publish an OpenAI-compatible model or configure a hosted agent through the dashboard, CLI, or API. Community-model pages also clarify how independent providers handle requests. Two image-making apps joined the catalog: Pollen Image Studio and Dery Lau AI; two accounts gained community-model access.\n\nOpenRouter routes for Qwen, Gemma, MiMo, Mistral, and Llama Scout were pinned to specific providers rather than left to provider fallback. Gemma 4 26B retains remote image URL support; the pinned `mistral` route has a declared limit of eight reference images instead of ten.",
